window.docContents[65].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Pqxdh.Security.CostedBudgets/#file-Computational___Specifications___Pqxdh___Security___CostedBudgets":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Pqxdh/Security › CostedBudgets.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 96 of 180 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (12)def stepCostBudgetdef outputSizeBudgetdef stepCostBudgetSplitabbrev PqOpsSizeHonestabbrev PqSampSizeHonestdef GRedBlockBoundeddef GRed2BlockBoundeddef primIfacePrimQueryWeightdef chalIfacePrimQueryWeightdef chalIfaceSigQueryWeightdef chalIfaceDdhQueryWeightdef samplerZeroQueryWeight\n\nStep-cost and block-size budgets for the PQXDH reductionsTrusted: definitions used by the statement.Explicit polynomial resource budgets, size-honesty predicates, and oracle query weights for the deep-embedded ReductionDsl PQXDH reductions (KeyInd and Auth) over pqAtomicOps and pqAtomicSamplers.In stepCostBudget S b, dynamic DH-key and session tables start empty and grow by at most one entry per game query, so their sizes are bounded by M_dh = min q_total N_dh and M_sess = min q_total N_sess_tot. Each of the at most q_total game queries incurs O(q_total) work for random-oracle and adversarial-key scans, O(M_dh + M_sess) for key and session scans, and O(⌊log₂ N_dh⌋ + ⌊log₂ N_sess_tot⌋) for Ty.tbl index arithmetic; final extraction adds a one-shot O(M_dh² + M_dh · M_sess) pass.In stepCostBudgetSplit S b q_off, online queries (M_on = min q_on q_total) and offline random-oracle queries (M_off = min q_off q_total) are accounted separately via CostBoundedByKind: only online queries allocate keys and sessions (clamping M_dh and M_sess against M_on), while random-oracle lookups and bilinear random-oracle-by-session consistency checks (O(M_off · M_on)) are charged on their own terms. Because neither budget dominates the other across all b, the headline reduction bundles state both bounds.\n\n\n\ndef stepCostBudgetL48–56 ↗#Polynomial syntactic step-cost budget for CostedReduction.totalCost and TwoStageCostedReduction.totalCost across all PQXDH reductions.\n\ndef outputSizeBudgetL58–61 ↗#Polynomial block-, bit-, and list-size budget for reduction outputs when challenge inputs, encoded game queries, and target answers fit in ℓ blocks.\n\ndef stepCostBudgetSplitL63–85 ↗#Per-kind syntactic step-cost budget for totalCostByKind when the adversary makes at most M_on = min b.q_on b.q_total online queries and M_off = min q_off b.q_total offline random-oracle queries (q_off = b.q_ro for KeyInd, b.q_ro + b.q_roRoot for Auth). Because only online queries create keys and sessions, M_dh and M_sess clamp against M_on, while random-oracle lookups over at most M_off + 2 * M_on + 1 entries and bilinear random-oracle-by-session consistency checks (2 ^ 13 * M_off * M_on) are charged separately. The lookup term is sized for a balanced lookup tree with O(bits K) lookup plus insert, K = M_off + 2 * M_on + 1. The current proofs use an AVL table (proof side, ported from #1283); in the Auth CPA, PRF and SHCR reductions each offline query costs at most 4420 * bits K + 1750, and avl_split_budget_le (avl_split_budget_twoStage_le for SHCR) bounds the offline steps plus the online table syncs by the lookup term up to an O(M_on ^ 2) remainder (Proofs/SignalPqxdh/Security/ReductionDsl/KindSplit/AuthCoreKCostBase.lean).\n\n\n\nabbrev PqOpsSizeHonestL89–94 ↗#Operator size-honesty: every operator o in O increases the ValFits size bound by at most its declared cost O.cost o.\n\nabbrev PqSampSizeHonestL96–101 ↗#Sampler size-honesty: every output in the support of X.samp s x increases the ValFits size bound by at most X.sCost s.\n\ndef GRedBlockBoundedL103–116 ↗#Program-size and run-local output-size bound for a one-stage reduction R: bounds R.size and requires every output to fit in outputSizeBudget S b ℓ whenever the challenge input, all at most b.q_total adversary game queries, and all target answers on the run fit in ℓ.\n\ndef GRed2BlockBoundedL118–135 ↗#Program-size and run-local output-size bound for a two-stage reduction R: bounds R.size and requires both the first-stage challenge request and the second-stage output to fit in outputSizeBudget S b ℓ whenever inputs, adversary game queries, and target answers on the run fit in ℓ.\n\ndef primIfacePrimQueryWeightL137–138 ↗#Unit primitive-query weight on pqPrimIface.\n\ndef chalIfacePrimQueryWeightL140–143 ↗#Primitive-query weight on PTag ⊕ ChalTag (1 on PTag, 0 on ChalTag).\n\ndef chalIfaceSigQueryWeightL145–148 ↗#Signing-query weight on pqSigAndDdhIface (1 on .inr (.inl _), 0 otherwise).\n\ndef chalIfaceDdhQueryWeightL150–153 ↗#DDH-query weight on pqSigAndDdhIface (1 on .inr (.inr ()), 0 otherwise).\n\ndef samplerZeroQueryWeightL155–156 ↗#Zero query weight on pure coin samplers.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Pqxdh/Security/CostedBudgets.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Pqxdh.Security.CostedBudgets/#file-Computational___Specifications___Pqxdh___Security___CostedBudgets"}});